If you win,

293
00:10:11,346 --> 00:10:13,724
you collect one hundred dollars.

294
00:10:13,724 --> 00:10:14,583
If you lose,

295
00:10:14,583 --> 00:10:16,064
you get nothing.

296
00:10:16,094 --> 00:10:17,048
Either way,

297
00:10:17,048 --> 00:10:19,361
the toll was paid at the start.

298
00:10:19,617 --> 00:10:21,091
For the whole market,

299
00:10:21,091 --> 00:10:23,226
the regulator put the numbers in

300
00:10:23,226 --> 00:10:24,467
perspective.

301
00:10:24,807 --> 00:10:27,672
Twenty-five billion dollars of event

302
00:10:27,672 --> 00:10:30,277
contracts in a month sounds huge.

303
00:10:30,557 --> 00:10:32,750
But it is about zero point zero

304
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:35,162
eight percent of all the futures trading

305
00:10:35,162 --> 00:10:37,297
the commission oversees.

306
00:10:37,517 --> 00:10:38,632
Small for Wall Street,

307
00:10:38,632 --> 00:10:41,818
enormous for a product that barely existed

308
00:10:41,818 --> 00:10:43,555
a few years ago.

309
00:10:43,817 --> 00:10:46,337
Let me draw the business model.

310
00:10:46,457 --> 00:10:47,450
On one side,

311
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:50,077
thousands of traders with hunches.

312
00:10:50,077 --> 00:10:51,195
In the middle,

313
00:10:51,195 --> 00:10:52,085
the exchange,

314
00:10:52,085 --> 00:10:54,967
taking a small toll on every match.

315
00:10:55,167 --> 00:10:56,474
On the other side,

316
00:10:56,474 --> 00:10:57,781
the market makers,

317
00:10:57,781 --> 00:10:59,267
earning the spread.

318
00:10:59,477 --> 00:11:01,228
The traders win and lose against each

319
00:11:01,228 --> 00:11:02,217
other.

320
00:11:02,247 --> 00:11:04,043
The toll booth is the only one

321
00:11:04,043 --> 00:11:06,887
that collects on every single trade.

322
00:11:07,150 --> 00:11:09,695
So how do prediction markets make money

323
00:11:09,695 --> 00:11:11,220
off your hunches?

324
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:13,540
Not by betting against you.

325
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,984
By charging a small fee every time

326
00:11:15,984 --> 00:11:16,629
you trade,

327
00:11:16,629 --> 00:11:18,630
most of all when nobody is sure

328
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:20,120
what will happen.

329
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,794
Whether that makes them a financial market

330
00:11:22,794 --> 00:11:24,939
or a casino is a question the

331
00:11:24,939 --> 00:11:27,040
courts are still fighting over.

332
00:11:27,090 --> 00:11:29,423
But the toll booth gets paid either

333
00:11:29,423 --> 00:11:30,315
way.

334
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:32,552
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

335
00:11:32,552 --> 00:11:34,940
we follow the money behind another hidden

336
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:36,880
link of the world economy.

337
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:39,053
This is The Hidden Economics.
